// +gobra

package resalgebra

// This package shows that we can provide a model for ghost locations, similar to
// those of Iris entirely in Gobra. All lemmas in the interface RA are universally
// quantified (rather than requiring the user to provide instantiations of the
// quantified variables), and all lemmas for ghost locations are formulated in
// terms of an explicit Witness value. This is due to a technicality in Gobra:
// we cannot existentially quantify over resources.

// To keep the public API for ghost locations free of witnesses, `uniqueloc.gobra`
// bundles a location name and its witness into the type `UniqueLoc`, whose
// fields are both unexported. The public predicate `GhostLocation` and the
// public operations (`Alloc`, `GhostOp1`, `GhostOp2`, `GhostValid`,
// `GhostUpdate`) are stated in terms of `UniqueLoc` and are thin, *proven*
// wrappers around the witness-based operations of `loc.gobra`. In particular,
// the public API introduces no additional assumptions.
